# The patched RTX 50 kernels (sm86/build.py --arch sm_120) that have run on an RTX 50 card, one line each:
#   <nvcc version> <hash> <what ran it>
# build.py writes qc_sm120_cubin.h only when what it built is listed here for the nvcc that built it, so a toolkit
# that compiles the kernel another way ships no patched kernel and the core runs the compiled one. The hash covers
# every section of the cubin but the names, so one line serves Linux and Windows builds (qc_sm86.ref says more).
# A line is added only after its file has run verify-core.js (all five checks) on an RTX 50 card through
# QUANTUS_CUDA_CUBIN_FILE, and the core's own startup check has passed there.

# QC_RED 3 on sm_120 (goal/q4-rtx50 f5b51a35, 21 Nov; no longer built, d61fd20c's lines below replace them): 504 tails, 21 partial rounds unrolled, 2 blocks of 384.
# Linux and Windows cubins differ outside the code (build.py's "code alone" hash is the same, 90c9ce3507494f41 for
# 12.8 and 4cc8f07636923319 for 13.3), so each toolkit has two lines. RTX 5070 (Salad llmjob2 PC aed133e3, driver
# 621.24, 250 W), Linux files through QUANTUS_CUDA_CUBIN_FILE in qrace.sh: startup check passed, verify-core all five
# PASS on both cores (438.44 and 449.26 MH/s). Live on HeroMiners against #317's head 29426bda on the same PC, clock
# held at 2,775 MHz: 12.8 core 436.20 against 414.59, CUDA 13 core 447.15 / 447.35 against 425.49 / 425.36 (+5.1%).
