# goal/q5-nv50 (28 Nov): QC_RED 4, the reduction as four adds with no multiply, its third add's carry-in inverted and
# pairs of two-input adds fused in place by sm120/fuse.py (504 tails; 325 pairs with 12.8, 315 with 13.3). Code alone
# 1bee24fbca8871ba (12.8) and 178d38870199c105 (13.3) on Linux and Windows. Linux files through QUANTUS_CUDA_CUBIN_FILE
# in qrace.sh on an RTX 5070 (Salad llmjob2 PC d0bbecea, driver 621.24, 250 W, power-bound) and an RTX 5060 (driver
# 616): startup check passed and verify-core all five PASS on both cores on both cards. Live on HeroMiners against
# #317's head 72b94c90 on the RTX 5070: 12.8 core 509.02 / 506.98 against 470.74 / 471.03 (+7.9%), CUDA 13 core
# 507.27 / 507.25 against 471.24 / 471.06 (+7.7%); SRBMiner 3.8.9 620.73 / 621.53.
# On the RTX 5060 the CUDA 13 core ran 296.40 / 296.67 against 275.44 / 275.15 (+7.7%; SRBMiner 363.88), but the 12.8
# core 257.74 / 256.78 against 260.19 / 260.74 (-1.3%). So build.py makes this kernel with CUDA 13 only; the 12.8
# lines below are what --defs -DQC_FUSE=1 builds, and the 12.8 core keeps d61fd20c's kernel above.
